<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS TRACKER MUSIC AND HOW DID IT EVOLVE</pattern>
<template>Tracker music is a type of music used in the Amiga game industry, originally developed by 1001 Crew and The Judges. It evolved into various formats such as S3M, XM, IT, and OpenMPT. Tracker music has influenced broader internet music culture, including blog-era genres like bloghouse, blog rock, and blog rap in the early 2000s.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT ARE KEY FEATURES OF TRACKER MUSIC</pattern>
<template>Tracker music is characterized by its modular structure, with each module file containing a single instrument or sound effect. It is often used in video game development, with notable examples including Jaakko Iisalo's Angry Birds and Unity Technologies' Renaldas Zioma and Erik Hemming.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT ARE DIFFERENT FORMATS OF TRACKER MUSIC</pattern>
<template>Tracker music can be distributed in various formats, including S3M (Scream Tracker 3), XM (FastTracker 2), IT (Impulse Tracker), and OpenMPT. These formats are used to create different types of music, such as synth-pop, chiptune, and vaporwave.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS TIMELINE OF TRACKER MUSIC S PROMINENCE IN INTERNET MUSIC SCENE</pattern>
<template>Tracker music's prominence in the internet music scene is gradual, beginning in the late 1980s/early 1990s rather than being a sudden post-2000 phenomenon.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT ARE SOME NOTABLE DEMOSCENE MUSICIANS WHO WORKED IN VIDEO GAME DEVELOPMENT</pattern>
<template>Notable demoscene musicians who worked in video game development include Jaakko Iisalo (Angry Birds) and Unity Technologies' Renaldas Zioma and Erik Hemming.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT ARE SOME EXAMPLES OF TRACKER MUSIC USED IN VIDEO GAME DEVELOPMENT</pattern>
<template>Examples of tracker music used in video game development include Jaakko Iisalo's Angry Birds and Unity Technologies' Renaldas Zioma and Erik Hemming.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT ARE SOME EXAMPLES OF TRACKER MUSIC USED IN NON GAME CONTEXTS</pattern>
<template>Tracker music has also influenced non-game contexts and genres such as chiptune and vaporwave.</template>
</category>
